    {
      "id": "evidence-000-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "Anchored on `certified=1 outcome=verified` in one row of `certified_implies_revalidatable`, which re-validates against a FRESH PARSE of the SMT-LIB text rather than the producing run's arena. That distinction is the whole point of the anchor: checking against the producer's own arena passes for any certificate, including one that merely copies the producer's conclusions. `UnsatQuantInstanceSet` shipped `certified=1` over a FAILED re-check on 2026-08-17 because its TermIds meant nothing in a second arena, and this suite exists because of it.",
